see 2 General Restrictions.
● The source operand address must not overlap the destination operand
address.
● The address of sharedTmpBuffer must not overlap the addresses of the
source operand and destination operand.
● Currently, only the ND format is supported.
● For Mean, the approach used is to first calculate the sum and then perform
division. The underlying addition method used by Mean is consistent with that
employed by Sum, ReducceSum, and WholeReducceSum, both of which
utilize a binary tree approach to add two elements at a time. For details, refer
to Sum.
